
Shared libraries in cado-nfs
----------------------------

cado-nfs can use dynamically linkable (shared) libraries, but this is
disabled by default, and must be requested with the ENABLE_SHARED=1
environment variable. In the particular case of cross-compiling, it is
preferrable to leave shared libraries disabled in order to avoid the
annoyance of debugging the related issues. When ENABLE_SHARED is not set,
gf2x is configured with --disable-shared as well. For a fully static
build, also set:

LDFLAGS=-static

Extra flags for the gf2x configure script can be passed with
GF2X_CONFIGURE_EXTRA_FLAGS="whichever;flags;you;want;to;pass;to;gf2x;configure;separated;by;semicolons"
